{
  "Arranges tiles of different sizes on a grid of base cells, where each tile spans a set number of cells. Tiles fill the height in columns and scroll horizontally, or fill the width in rows. They can be selected and reordered by dragging.": "",
  "Tile grid": "",
  "`baseItemWidth` and `baseItemHeight` define one cell, and a tile's `widthRatio` and `heightRatio` set how many cells it spans. In the default `horizontal` direction, the view needs a `height` and scrolls horizontally. Tiles are packed so that no cell stays empty where a later tile fits.": "",
  "Selecting tiles": "",
  "`selectionMode` makes tiles selectable. `single` keeps one selected, and `multiple` allows any number (Ctrl + click or Space adds and removes). `value` is the `key` or index of the selected tile, or a list of them, and `x-model` provides two-way binding. The arrow keys move through the grid based on tile positions.": "",
  "Reordering": "",
  "With `allowReorder`, users can drag a tile to a new position (a long press on a touch screen) or move it with Ctrl and an arrow key. The tile moves and `onReordered` reports the indexes. Reorder your data there, as the example does, so the next render matches.": "",
  "An item's `content` creates the tile content when the tile is created, and it behaves the same as anywhere else. A click on a button inside goes to that button. `onItemClick` reports a click on the tile itself.": "",
  "One Tab stop: the tile focused last, otherwise the first selected tile, otherwise the first tile.": "",
  "Moves to the nearest tile in that direction, based on tile positions. Home and End move to the first and last tile.": "",
  "Selects the tile (`single`), or toggles it (`multiple`).": "",
  "Acts as a click on the tile: raises `onItemClick` and applies the selection.": "",
  "With `allowReorder`, moves the tile one position back or forward. Ctrl + Home and End move it to the ends, and each move is announced.": "",
  "A `list` of `listitem` elements without selection, or a `listbox` of `option` elements with it (`aria-multiselectable` for `multiple`), each with `aria-selected`.": "",
  "`aria-disabled`. The tile is skipped by the keyboard and cannot be selected with a click.": "",
  "A copy of the tile follows the pointer, the tile at the drop position is marked, and Escape cancels. On a touch screen, a long press lifts the tile.": "",
  "The view. `data-direction`, `data-reorder`, and `data-dragging` while a tile is dragged.": "",
  "A tile. `aria-selected`, `aria-disabled`, `data-dragging` (shown faded in place), and `data-drop=\"before|after\"` at the drop position.": "",
  "The tile text, and the copy that follows the pointer.": "",
  "Units: a tile (`hover`, `pressed`, `focus`, `selected`, `disabled`, `dragging`, `target`), its text, the drag copy and the view.": "",
  "The gap between tiles.": "",
  "The tiles in order: `TileViewItem` objects (`text`, `widthRatio`, `heightRatio`, `key`, `content`, `enabled`, `data`) or plain text.": "",
  "The size of a base cell in pixels. A tile spans `widthRatio` × `heightRatio` cells.": "",
  "`horizontal` fills the height in columns and scrolls horizontally (set a `height`). `vertical` fills the width in rows.": "",
  "`none`, `single` or `multiple`.": "`none`, `single` ya da `multiple`.",
  "The selected tile (`single`), identified by its `key` or index, or a list of selected tiles (`multiple`). `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "Lets users reorder tiles by dragging or with Ctrl and an arrow key.": "",
